  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kiritkumar Gordhanbhai Patel, Food ... vs State Of Gujarat on 18 April, 2024 N R/Cr.Ma/5656/2021 Order DATED: 18/04/2024 IN THE HIGH COURT OF GUJARAT AT AHMEDABAD R/CRIMINAL MISC.APPLICATION (FOR LEAVE TO APPEAL) NO. 5656 of 2021 With R/CRIMINAL APPEAL NO. 889 of 2024 ========================================================== KIRITKUMAR GORDHANBHAI PATEL, FOOD SAFETY OFFICER, SURAT MUNICIPAL CORPORATION Versus STATE OF GUJARAT & ANR. ========================================================== Appearance: MR DEVANG BHATT FOR MR HS MUNSHAW(495) for the Applicant(s) No. 1 MR UTPAL M PANCHAL(1075) for the Respondent(s) No. 2 MS VRUNDA SHAH, ADDL.PUBLIC PROSECUTOR for the Respondent(s) No. 1 ========================================================== CORAM:HONOURABLE MRS. JUSTICE M. K. THAKKER Date : 18/04/2024 ORAL ORDER ORDER IN R/CRIMINAL MISC.APPLICATION (FOR LEAVE TO APPEAL) NO. 5656 of 2021",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "advocate Mr.Devang Bhatt submits that the judgment and order of acquittal was passed by the learned trial Court mainly on the ground that Rules 2.4.1(8)(13) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 was not followed by the complainant. Learned advocate Mr.Bhatt submits that as per Rule 2.4.1(13) it is mandatory that nature and quantity of preservative added shall be clearly noted on the label to be fixed to the container. 2.Learned advocate Mr.Bhatt submits that as per the Panch Witness as well as from the evidence of the complainant, it transpires that though all procedures prescribed under the Act was followed, learned trial Court has acquitted the respondent-accused."
  },
